8) What are the types of Dependency Injection?
      There are mainly 2 types of Dependency Injection in Spring Boot 
      - Constructor Injection
      - Setter Injection
      Constructor Injection is generally prefered because dependencies are provided at object creation time and are mandatory.

9) Constructor injection
      Construcor Injection is a Dependency Injection technique in Spring Boot where dependencies are provided
      through the constructor at the time of object creation.
                              or
      - Dependencies are provided to the dependent class through its constructor
      - Dependencies are passed as arguments to the constructor when the dependent class is instantiated
      - Constructor injection ensures that the dependencies are available when the object is created

10) Setter Injection
      Setter injection means injecting a dependency using a setter method and the @Autowired annotation. 
      Spring creates the object first, then calls the setter method to inject the dependency.


11) What is IOC
