14) Understanding Components and ComponentScan
      Component
      ==========
            Component refers to a java class that is managed by the SPring IOC container.
            @Component is an annotation used to tell Spring that a class is a Spring Bean and should be managed by Spring IOC Container.
            @Component is used to mark a class as a Spring-managed bean so that Spring can automatically create and manage its object.
            Defining Components in Spring :
            ------------------------------
                  - USing XML
                  - Using Annotations
      
                  Using XML
                  ---------
                        <bean id="myCompoent" class="com.example.MyComponent"/>
       
                  Using Annotation
                  ----------------
                        import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
      
                        @Component //Marks the class a Spring Component
                        public class MyComponent {
                              //Class implementation
                        }
      
      Component Scanning
      ==================
            - Component Scanning is a feature helps to automatically detect and register beans from predefined package paths.
            - @componentScan is used to scan packages for Spring components and register them as beans in the Spring container.
            - @ComponentScan is used to tell sPring where to search for classes annotated with:
                  * @Component
                  * @Service
                  * @Repository
                  * @Controller
             After finding them, spring automatically creates beans and stores them in the IOC container.


15) @Value Annotation
      - @Value is used to inject values from properties files, environment variables, or hardcoded values into a Spring bean.
      - @Value is used to read and inject values from application.properties or application.yml into java variables.

      Ex:
            application.properties
                  app.name=Student Management System
            Java class
                  @Component
                  public class AppInfo {
                  
                      @Value("${app.name}")
                      private String appName;
                  
                      public void display() {
                          System.out.println(appName);
                      }
                  }
            Output :
                  StudentManagement System

            Hardcoded Value
            ---------------
                  @Value("Hello Spring Boot")
                  private String message;

            Default Value
            ------------
                  @Value("${server.port:8080}")
                  private int port;
      

16) @Autowired Annotation
      - @Autowired is used for Dependency Injection (DI). It tells Spring automatically provide the required bean object.
      - @Autowired is used to automatically inject one Spring bean into another bean.

17) @Qualifier Annotation
      - @Qualifier is used along with @Autowired to specify which bean should be injected when multiple beans of the same type are available.
      - @Qualifier is used to resolve the ambiguity when more than one bean of the same type exists in the Spring container.

18) What is Spring Boot?
      - Open-source, java-based framework used to create stand-alone production-guide Spring-based Application.
      - Spring Boot is an extension of the Spring framework that simplifies Java application development. It provides auto-configuration, starter dependencies,
         and embedded servers, which help developers build production-ready applications quickly with minimal configuration.

            Spring Boot = Spring Framework + prebuilt Configuration + Embedded Servers
